    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Zs_K50vivDF5"
      },
      "source": [
        "#### Changing, adding, and removing elements"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5q6K1NTNvDF5"
      },
      "source": [
        "A list can change after it is created: assign to an index to **replace** an element, and use the list methods to add or remove elements.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Operation        | What it does                                                    |\n",
        "| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n",
        "| `a[i] = x`       | replace the element at index `i`                                |\n",
        "| `a.append(x)`    | add `x` at the **end**                                          |\n",
        "| `a.insert(i, x)` | add `x` at index `i`; the elements after it shift one place     |\n",
        "| `a.remove(x)`    | remove the **first** element equal to `x`                       |\n",
        "| `a.pop()`        | remove the **last** element and give it back (`a.pop(i)`: at i) |\n",
        "| `x in a`         | `True` if `x` is somewhere in the list, otherwise `False`       |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 11,
      "metadata": {
