      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "True\n",
            "False\n",
            "74 °C recorded 3 times\n",
            "First time at 74 °C: 12:00\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# search_temps.py\n",
        "temps = [\n",
        "    61, 60, 60, 59, 59, 60,   # 00:00–05:00\n",
        "    63, 66, 69, 71, 72, 73,   # 06:00–11:00\n",
        "    74, 74, 75, 74, 73, 72,   # 12:00–17:00\n",
        "    70, 68, 66, 64, 63, 62,   # 18:00–23:00\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(75 in temps)                         # True: it reached 75 °C\n",
        "print(80 in temps)                         # False: it never reached 80 °C\n",
        "print(\"74 °C recorded\", temps.count(74), \"times\")\n",
        "print(\"First time at 74 °C:\", str(temps.index(74)) + \":00\")   # FIRST position"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PbGMFifGvDGD"
      },
      "source": [
        "> **index() needs the value to exist**\n",
        ">\n",
        "> `temps.index(80)` stops the program with a `ValueError`, because 80 is not in the list. Check with\n",
        "> `80 in temps` first when you are not sure."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "o82NFgWzvDGD"
      },
      "source": [
        "#### Sorting without breaking the original data"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "u6cxcEojvDGE"
      },
      "source": [
        "`sorted(a)` makes a **new** sorted list; the hourly order in `temps` stays intact. `a.sort()` sorts **the list itself**, so use it on a copy (`.copy()`). From sorted data the middle value (**median**) is easy to read: for 24 values, the median is the average of the two middle values (indices 11 and 12)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 17,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "1V57jeSavDGE",
        "outputId": "a9ae10c9-b418-4cc7-a032-b13f70b0c658"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Lowest 3 : [59, 59, 60]\n",
            "Highest 3: [74, 74, 75]\n",
            "Original : [61, 60, 60]\n",
            "Median   : 67.0 °C\n",
            "Largest first: [75, 74, 74, 74, 73]\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# sort_temps.py\n",
        "temps = [\n",
        "    61, 60, 60, 59, 59, 60,   # 00:00–05:00\n",
        "    63, 66, 69, 71, 72, 73,   # 06:00–11:00\n",
        "    74, 74, 75, 74, 73, 72,   # 12:00–17:00\n",
        "    70, 68, 66, 64, 63, 62,   # 18:00–23:00\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "ordered = sorted(temps)                # a NEW sorted list\n",
        "print(\"Lowest 3 :\", ordered[:3])\n",
        "print(\"Highest 3:\", ordered[-3:])\n",
        "print(\"Original :\", temps[:3])         # unchanged: still in hourly order\n",
        "\n",
        "median = (ordered[11] + ordered[12]) / 2   # 24 values: the two in the middle\n",
        "print(\"Median   :\", median, \"°C\")\n",
        "\n",
        "copy = temps.copy()                    # copy first...\n",
        "copy.sort(reverse=True)                # ...because sort() changes the list itself\n",
        "print(\"Largest first:\", copy[:5])"
      ]
    },
