    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rLch_VyXvDGe"
      },
      "source": [
        "| Mistake                               | What happens                                | Fix                                                     |\n",
        "| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n",
        "| Off by one: day _n_ at index `n`      | you get the next day, or an IndexError      | day _n_ is at index `n - 1`                             |\n",
        "| Using index `len(a)`                  | `IndexError: list index out of range`       | the last index is `len(a) - 1` (or `a[-1]`)             |\n",
        "| `range(1, len(a))` by accident        | the first element is skipped                | start at 0, unless you really need the previous element |\n",
        "| Changing a list while looping over it | some elements are skipped                   | build a new list (filter) instead                       |\n",
        "| Forgetting `append` returns nothing   | `a = a.append(5)` makes `a` equal to `None` | just call `a.append(5)`                                 |\n",
        "| Expecting a slice to change the list  | `a[1:3]` is a new list; `a` is unchanged    | assign the slice to a variable                          |\n",
        "\n",
        "The fourth mistake is sneaky because nothing crashes. See it for yourself:"
      ]
